Solid State Physics — David Tong (@mat-tong-solid: 0, is #reference, #part-of @mat-sources) { r_2G2CQ9C5QDEBTQ2YNMYQ5QK3MB
David Tong, University of Cambridge, Lent 2017. [Course and four problem sheets](https://davidtong.org/teaching/solid-state-physics/), [complete 131-page notes](https://davidtong.org/pdfs/teaching/solid-state-physics/solidstate.pdf).

Read the four chapters in full: quantum motion in magnetic fields, bands, electron dynamics and phonons. The materials route introduces the necessary concepts progressively and returns to the magnetic chapter later. Contents and selected Bloch/reciprocal-lattice passages were inspected on 30 October 2026. This is not a complete engineering treatment of ferromagnetic devices. Use the magnetic source and application studies alongside it. Freely readable author-hosted notes; no general adaptation licence was established. Keep the PDF external.

**Return:** [Materials-engineering sources — reading and primary evidence](../Sources.lingua#r_51JAH6DB4WV2HZAB69G21ZHSMK).
